# Wayfarer Meadow: the Bent Spoon Inn under its thatch and chimney, and the old wayfarers' oak.
# Hand-placed by the landmark pass on the room's blocked back band and what lies behind it,
# so it never stands on a tile a knight walks or hides the floor from the camera.

# the inn: whitewashed ground floor, jettied timber above, a thatch roof and a chimney
box    plaster at 84 0 -2 size 84 26 28 id lm-inn
box    wood    at 84 26 -1 size 90 16 29
gable  thatch  at 84 42 -1 size 96 22 34
box    brick   at 112 42 -6 size 9 24 9
box    door    at 84 0 12.5 size 12 20 2
box    wood    at 36 18 15 size 2 16 2
box    wood    at 28 22 15 size 14 10 1.5
# the old oak at the road's end
cylinder-10 trunk   at 312 0 -4 size 12 34 12 id lm-oak-trunk
blob-5 foliage at 312 22 -4 size 78 46 40 id lm-oak-crown
